step Noonshade Ruins: kill these as you meet them
  zone Tanaris
  tip Ride back west toward Gadgetzan. The Wastewander bandits and thieves hold the dunes on the way; any of them can carry a water pouch.
  tip Careful: Wastewander Rogues (level 43-44) move stealthed, so they can approach unseen.
  kill 5616 quest 1690                -- Wastewander Thief
  collect 8483 quest 1707             -- Wastewander Water Pouch
  kill 5618 quest 1690                -- Wastewander Bandit

step Gadgetzan
  turnin 1707                         -- Spigot Operator Luglunket
  turnin 1690                         -- Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
  accept 1691

step Waterspring Field
  tip The tougher Wastewander rogues, shadow mages and assassins camp south-east of Gadgetzan, south of the bandits. Leave Caliph Scorpidsting in the middle of the southern camp for later.
  tip Careful: Wastewander Rogues keep Sneak up while out of combat, so hidden rogues can join a fight you start at a camp.
  kill 5617 quest 1691                -- Wastewander Shadow Mage
  collect 8483 x5
  kill 5615 quest 1691                -- Wastewander Rogue
  kill 5623 quest 1691                -- Wastewander Assassin

step Lost Rigger Cove: kill these as you meet them
  zone Tanaris
  tip Follow the coast south to the pirate cove. Southsea pirates crowd the beach and the boats: work along the edge and pull one at a time. Andre Firebeard stands on the far side; Stoley's stolen cargo lies in the camp.
  tip Careful: Two or three pirates stand with Andre, and many more pirates from the town join the fight once it starts.
  kill 7855 quest 8366                -- Southsea Pirate
  collect 20519 quest 8365            -- Southsea Pirate Hat
  kill 7856 quest 8366                -- Southsea Freebooter
  kill 7858 quest 8366                -- Southsea Swashbuckler
  collect 9244 x1 quest 2873          -- Stoley's Shipment; upstairs
  kill 7857 quest 8366                -- Southsea Dock Worker
  collect 9246 x1 quest 2875          -- Firebeard's Head

